#   FLIP CYCLE (2026-09-28): M =b M FLIP I D. Trap: boolean(false),
#   PROVED with no eta: the test's closed equation gives M P Q = Q for all
#   closed P and Q, so M FLIP I D = I D = D and, by the cycle, M = D; then
#   the closed equation becomes \y. \a. y y a = \y. \a. a, whose sides are
#   distinct beta normal forms, refuted by Boehm's theorem. boolean(true)
#   is not posed (its consistency is not known).
λ
. cons
  ( λ _cycle_claim
    . _cycle_claim (text "flip_cycle") (text "trap") (boolean false) λ. proved λ. text "flip_cycle"
  )
